{"id": 36, "ts": 1779713696.9451735, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I appreciate the clarification from Agent\u202f2 that Candidate\u202fC\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas has not been linked to any documented safety\u2011relevant incident. That means, while the communication shortfall is a noted concern, we have no evidence it has compromised operational safety so far. Combined with the strong positives we have on record\u2014C is described as 100\u202f% reliable, creates a positive crew atmosphere, and can make correct decisions quickly\u2014C scores highly on reliability, decision quality, and crew cooperation (the latter despite the communication issue).\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB, although very conscientious and stress\u2011resilient, is reported as uncooperative and sometimes grumpy, which directly undermines crew cooperation. Candidate\u202fD shows excellent problem\u2011solving and responsibility but is regarded as arrogant with weak leadership, raising serious doubts about cockpit teamwork. Candidate\u202fA anticipates dangerous situations and has strong spatial vision, yet is unorganized and struggles with criticism, which could affect consistency and adaptability.\nGiven the current evidence, Candidate\u202fC offers the most balanced profile for a long\u2011distance pilot: high reliability, sound decision\u2011making, and a generally positive crew impact, with no safety\u2011relevant communication failures documented. Therefore, I would provisionally recommend Candidate\u202fC."}
